Add `CheckerPool.Release(Program)`. A client that will not verify a program again can
make the idle checkers last set up for it forget it and drop their prover's managed
context, including the VC variables its translator keeps for every program's globals and
locals, so that the program and its variables can be collected. The solver is sent nothing and gets the
same commands with or without a release; no option is added and no output changes.
